1
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:16,278
On the fifth day-- again, as always, it was thanks to the sheep--

2
00:00:16,278 --> 00:00:21,500
the secret of the little prince's life was revealed to me.

3
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,940
Abruptly, without anything to lead up to it, and as if the question had been born

4
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:31,159
of long and silent meditation on his problem, he demanded:

5
00:00:31,159 --> 00:00:37,819
"A sheep-- if it eats little bushes, does it eat flowers, too?"

6
00:00:37,819 --> 00:00:44,058
"A sheep," I answered, "eats anything it finds in its reach."

7
00:00:44,058 --> 00:00:47,839
"Even flowers that have thorns?"

8
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:52,038
"Yes, even flowers that have thorns."

9
00:00:52,038 --> 00:00:57,019
"Then the thorns-- what use are they?"

10
00:00:57,019 --> 00:01:00,619
I did not know but that moment I was very busy trying

11
00:01:00,619 --> 00:01:03,798
to unscrew a bolt that had got stuck in my engine.

12
00:01:03,798 --> 00:01:07,640
I was very much worried, for it was becoming clear to me that the breakdown

13
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:10,099
of my plane was extremely serious.

14
00:01:10,099 --> 00:01:15,519
And I had so little drinking water left that I had to fear the worst

15
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:21,798
thorns-- what use are they?"

16
00:01:21,798 --> 00:01:26,058
The little prince never let go of a question, once he had asked it.

17
00:01:26,058 --> 00:01:30,859
As for me, I was upset over that bolt. And I answered with the first thing that

18
00:01:30,859 --> 00:01:36,319
came into my head: "The thorns are of no use at all

19
00:01:36,319 --> 00:01:40,579
if I was have thorns just for spite!"

20
00:01:40,579 --> 00:01:43,240
"Oh!"

21
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:46,819
There was a moment of complete silence.

22
00:01:46,819 --> 00:01:51,798
Then little prince flashed back at me, with a kind of resentfulness:

23
00:01:51,798 --> 00:01:57,558
"I don't believe you! Flowers are weak creatures. They are naive. They reassure

24
00:01:57,558 --> 00:01:59,298
themselves as best they can.

25
00:01:59,298 --> 00:02:03,558
They believe that their thorns are terrible weapons..."

26
00:02:03,558 --> 00:02:05,898
I did not answer.

27
00:02:05,898 --> 00:02:11,480
At that instant I was saying to myself: "If this bolt still won't turn I'm going

28
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:14,480
to knock it out with the hammer."

29
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:19,099
Again the little prince disturbed my thoughts.

30
00:02:19,099 --> 00:02:23,778
"And you actually believe that the flowers have Oh, no!"

31
00:02:23,778 --> 00:02:26,058
I cried. "No, no no!

32
00:02:26,058 --> 00:02:30,558
I don't believe anything. I answered you with the first thing that came into my

33
00:02:30,558 --> 00:02:36,919
head. Don't you see-- I am very busy with matters of consequence!"

34
00:02:36,919 --> 00:02:41,859
He stared at me, thunderstruck.

35
00:02:41,859 --> 00:02:45,919
"Matters of consequence!"

36
00:02:45,919 --> 00:02:50,359
He looked at me there, with my hammer in my hand, my fingers black with engine

37
00:02:50,359 --> 00:02:56,659
grease bending down over an object, which seemed to him extremely ugly...

38
00:02:56,659 --> 00:03:00,859
"You talk just like the grown-ups!"

39
00:03:00,859 --> 00:03:03,500
That made me a little ashamed.

40
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:10,519
But he went on, relentlessly: "You mix everything up together... You confuse everything..."

41
00:03:10,519 --> 00:03:16,038
He was really very angry. He tossed his golden curls in the breeze.

42
00:03:16,038 --> 00:03:20,240
"I know a planet whether there is a certain red-faced gentleman gears never

43
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:25,278
smelled a flower. He has never looked at a star. He has never loved anyone He has

44
00:03:25,278 --> 00:03:29,659
never done anything in his life but add up figures. And all day he says over and

45
00:03:29,659 --> 00:03:34,519
over, just like you: 'I am busy with matters of consequence!' And that makes

46
00:03:34,519 --> 00:03:36,619
him swell up with pride.

47
00:03:36,619 --> 00:03:43,398
But he is not a man-- he is a mushroom!"

48
00:03:43,398 --> 00:03:45,019
"A what?"

49
00:03:45,019 --> 00:03:47,298
"A mushroom!"

50
00:03:47,298 --> 00:03:53,298
The little prince was now white with rage flowers have been growing thorns for

51
00:03:53,298 --> 00:03:57,380
millions of years. For millions of years the sheep have been eating them just the

52
00:03:57,380 --> 00:04:01,639
same. And is it not a matter of consequence to try to understand why the

53
00:04:01,639 --> 00:04:06,440
flowers go to so much trouble to grow thorns, which are never of any use to them

54
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:11,059
it's the warfare between the sheep and the flowers not important? Is this not of

55
00:04:11,059 --> 00:04:16,159
more consequence than a fat red-faced gentleman's sums?

56
00:04:16,159 --> 00:04:23,179
And if I know-- I, myself-- one flower which is unique in the world, which grows

57
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:29,239
nowhere but on my planet, but but which one little sheep can destroy in a single

58
00:04:29,239 --> 00:04:35,079
bite some morning, without even noticing what he is doing-- Oh!

59
00:04:35,079 --> 00:04:38,898
You think that is not important!"

60
00:04:38,898 --> 00:04:46,159
His face turned from white to red as he continued: "If someone loves a flower, of which just

61
00:04:46,159 --> 00:04:50,780
one single blossom grows in all the millions and millions of stars, it is

62
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:54,980
enough to make him happy just to look at the stars.

63
00:04:54,980 --> 00:05:00,679
He can say to himself, 'Somewhere, my flower is there...'

64
00:05:00,679 --> 00:05:08,059
But if the sheep eats the flower, in one moment all his stars will be darkened

65
00:05:08,059 --> 00:05:13,480
did you think that is not important!"

66
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:18,079
He could not say anything more.

67
00:05:18,079 --> 00:05:22,719
His words were choked by sobbing.

68
00:05:23,358 --> 00:05:29,719
The night had fallen I'd let my tools drop from my hands.

69
00:05:29,719 --> 00:05:35,900
Of what importance now is my hammer, my bolt, or thirst, or death?

70
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:45,079
On one star, one planet, my planet, the Earth, there was a little prince to be comforted.

71
00:05:45,079 --> 00:05:48,858
I took him in my arms, and rocked him.

72
00:05:48,858 --> 00:05:51,760
I said to him:

73
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:55,579
"The flower that you love is not in danger.

74
00:05:55,579 --> 00:05:59,119
I will draw you a muzzle for your sheep.

75
00:05:59,119 --> 00:06:03,440
I will draw you a railing to put around your flower.

76
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:06,219
I will--"

77
00:06:07,039 --> 00:06:10,159
I did not know what to say to him.

78
00:06:10,159 --> 00:06:13,579
I felt awkward and blundering.

79
00:06:13,579 --> 00:06:17,960
I did not know how I could reach him, where I could overtake him and go on

80
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,760
hand in hand with him once more.

81
00:06:23,119 --> 00:06:26,920
It is such a secret place,

82
00:06:27,199 --> 00:06:30,760
the land of tears
